# Copy to .env.local and fill in.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ values ship in the browser bundle by design and are not secret.
# RESEND_API_KEY is a secret: it must never be given a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix, and
# .env.local is gitignored.

# Canonical origin, used for metadataBase, canonical URLs, robots.txt and the
# sitemap. No trailing slash, and no www - www should 301 to the apex so the
# two hosts do not compete for the same rankings.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://akdhospitality.com

# Where the 110 PDFs are served from. Defaults to /documents inside this repo.
# Point this at blob or object storage if the static payload ever needs to move
# off the deployment.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_DOCS_BASE_URL=/documents

# --- Contact form (Resend) ---------------------------------------------------
# Enquiries post to /api/contact, which sends the mail through Resend.
#
# Without RESEND_API_KEY the form still renders and validates, but submitting
# shows a notice asking the visitor to email us directly - it never silently
# drops a message.
#
# SECRET. Create it at https://resend.com/api-keys with Sending access only.
RESEND_API_KEY=

# Inbox that receives enquiries. Defaults to the address in src/data/company.ts.
#
# BEFORE THE DOMAIN IS VERIFIED this must be the address that owns the Resend
# account. Resend's sandbox sender refuses anything else:
#
#   403 "You can only send testing emails to your own email address (...).
#        To send emails to other recipients, please verify a domain at
#        resend.com/domains, and change the `from` address to an email using
#        this domain."
#
# So info@akdhospitality.com will NOT work yet - it is not deliverable until the
# domain exists and is verified. Point this at the account owner meanwhile.
# CONTACT_TO=info@akdhospitality.com

# Verified sender. Resend only accepts a domain verified at
# https://resend.com/domains; an unverified one returns
# 403 "The <domain> domain is not verified".
#
# Leave this unset until then: the route falls back to Resend's sandbox sender,
# which is the only sender allowed before verification.
#
# Once akdhospitality.com is verified, set BOTH of these together - the sender
# must be on the verified domain, and only then can CONTACT_TO be an address
# other than the account owner's.
# CONTACT_FROM=AKD Hospitality website <no-reply@akdhospitality.com>

# --- Database (admin dashboard) ----------------------------------------------
# Local PostgreSQL. Create the database once:
#   createdb -U postgres akd_hospitality
# then apply the schema and load the site's existing content:
#   npm run db:migrate
#   npm run db:seed
#
# SECRET (contains the password). Server only, never NEXT_PUBLIC_.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:PASSWORD@127.0.0.1:5432/akd_hospitality

# Signs the admin session cookie. Any long random string; changing it logs
# everyone out. Generate one with:  openssl rand -base64 32
# SECRET. Server only.
AUTH_SECRET=

# Dashboard uploads are written to ./storage. In production mount a volume
# there rather than configuring another path - the path is a literal so the
# build can scope its filesystem tracing.
